To design a suitable iterative scheme, we divide the approximation solutions into local, and non-local parts, and introduce a *localized corrector* for balancing the non-compact support and non-divergence form parts of the new tensor error. For the local and non-local parts, we construct different perturbations to proceed with the iteration.

1.  For given $u^{\text{loc}}_q$ with compact support, the local part of the approximate solution $u_q$, we construct the perturbation $w^\textup{loc}_{q+1}$ with devergence-free and compact-support, based on the intermittent building blocks in (BV; MY) such that $u^{\text{loc}}_{q+1}=u^{\text{loc}}_{\ell_q}+w^\textup{loc}_{q+1}$. More precisely, $w^\textup{loc}_{q+1}$ is composed by four parts:

    1.  The principle perturbation $w^{\textup{(p)}}_{q+1}$, which is constructed by using the box flows as in  (MY);

    2.  The incompressibility corrector $w^{\textup{(c)}}_{q+1}$, which is introduced to correct principal perturbation $w^{\textup{(p)}}_{q+1}$ to satisfy the incompressibility condition;

    3.  The temporal corrector $w^{\textup{(t)}}_{q+1}$. We design it for cancelling the extra errors with the traveling-wave property. To ensure that $w^{\textup{(t)}}_{q+1}$ has compact support, its construction is slightly different from that in (BV; MY) and it is not divergence-free.
